{
  "name": "1939_warsaw",
  "title": "Siege of Warsaw, Sept 1939",
  "notes": "Siege of Warsaw, 8-28 Sep 1939. Rosters rebuilt with real battalion-level names from Wikipedia 'Siege of Warsaw (1939)' opposing-forces table (German divisional components per Mitcham, German Order of Battle). Attacker = the 8. Armee western assault: the 4. Panzer-Division Vorhut (Reinhardt — the 8-9 Sep Ochota/Wola attacks from the SW, ~80 of ~220 tanks lost to Polish 75mm AT and barricades) + the five ID divisions of the 26 Sep general assault on the western districts (10/18/19/31/46, per the article: 'Western parts of the city were attacked by 5 German divisions'), the 46. ID components verified separately (IR 42/72/97, AR 114, Pz.Jg.52, Pi.88). Each ID is modeled at its full 1939 structure: 3 IR x 3 bns (I/II/III), 2 artillery Abteilungen (horse-towed, like the real 1939 ARs), Pz.Jg.Abt (37mm), Pi.Btl as infantry + engineer support, Aufkl.Abt as recon support (1939 IDs had no organic Flak — the single Flak-Bttr. rides with the Vorhut). Defender = Armia Warszawa (Czuma/Rommel, ~124-140k peak): the Wikipedia west + Praga sectors — 13/15/25/5/20/44/8 DP remnants x3 under-strength bns (org 40 = 2/3 of baseline 60; 13. DP's own 43. pp 'Bajonczykow/Bayonne Legion' serves as the Volunteer Workers' Bde; 44. DP at Warsaw = 145. pp + 144. pp det.; 8. DP = the 21. pp 'Dzieci Warszawy' under Sosabowski), Zbiorcza Cav Bde (Abraham; Podolian/Greater-Poland/Pomeranian elements), the 33-tank city detachment (27 Vickers/7TP/R-35 + 6 TK/TKS), DOW artillery (64 guns), 75mm wz.36 AT (the barricade fighters), AA (86 guns), the improvised 1./2. 'Defenders of Praga' regiments and the Straz Obywatelska civil guard. East-bank (Praga) units are included as city garrison since the whole province deploys in-game. Scale = real battalions: 75 v 44 (+22 synthesized HQs), a 26 Sep-style western assault.",
  "province": 3544,
  "dirs": [
    "W",
    "SW"
  ],
